@title Member Portal Login
@subtitle How sign-in works at Pinecrest Credit Union
@author Identity team
@date Draft, 2026-10-08

## Login flow
diagram login sequence title="Member portal login (OIDC with PKCE)"
login: user "User" user
login: browser "Browser" user
login: web "Web App" svc
login: auth "Auth Server" svc
login: profile "Profile API" svc
login: user -> browser : click Sign in
login: browser -> web : GET /login
login: web --> browser : 302 to /authorize with PKCE challenge
login: browser -> auth : GET /authorize
login: auth -> user : show login and MFA prompt
login: user -> auth : credentials + MFA code
login: auth --> browser : 302 to /callback with code
login: browser -> web : GET /callback with code
login: web -> auth : POST /token with code verifier
login: auth --> web : access token + ID token + refresh token
login: web -> profile : GET /me with bearer token
login: profile --> web : profile JSON
login: web --> browser : set session cookie, render dashboard

## Tokens
table = Token,Lifetime,Stored where; Access token,15 minutes,server-side session; ID token,15 minutes,server-side session; Refresh token,30 days,encrypted session store; Session cookie,12 hours,"browser (HttpOnly, Secure)"

## Security notes
- PKCE is mandatory.
- MFA is required for every member.
- Failed logins lock the account after 5 attempts.

!! Tokens must never be exposed to browser JavaScript or kept in browser storage.
